WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.820
Arima. Be quiet.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.040
Oh, sorry. Shall I make some tea?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.580
If I want some, I'll tell you.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.330
Is it because second term's starting?

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.260
Is it because of them?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.720
Is that why you're feeling grumpy, President?

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.860
You're calling me grumpy?

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.550
Have I done something to 
annoy you, Gero Akoya-kun?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.340
You only use my last name like that 
when you're feeling grumpy, President.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.520
I'm afraid you're wrong about that, Gero-kun.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.620
Oh, I know!

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.100
I'll bring out the dacquoise
I've been holding on to.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.500
No.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.500
No thank you.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.140
But at times like this...

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.030
What do you mean...

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.490
..."times like this"?

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.430
Oh... Well...

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.280
What is it?

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.740
I have had enough of this!

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.440
Members of the Caerula Adamas.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.880
Our Total Conquest of Earth's Lifeforms 
Project has reached a serious problem.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.900
We still have not identified the enemy,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.580
and they block every one of our plans.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.210
Our most recent plan, as well...

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.760
It means our present strategy is not effective.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.360
Aurite is correct.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.130
I cannot afford to waste any more of 
my precious Zundar Needles like this.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.000
We must fundamentally rethink our strategy.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.150
Precious?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.520
Fundamentally?

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.210
That's right!

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.570
Instead of waiting for them to appear, 
we shall go on the offensive!

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.410
Go on the offensive?

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.080
A new development awaits us!

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:12.880
Love is Stronger than Pride

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:19.250
It happened before, too. 
He does such weird things by himself.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.280
He really can't read the mood.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.880
Or maybe it's that he <i>doesn't</i> read the mood?

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.240
Yeah, could be...

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.450
<i>What are they talking about?</i>

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>No, </i>who<i> are they talking about?</i>

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.790
<b>Makuwa Uriya</b>

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.380
<i>What kind of person must one be</i>

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.250
<i>to come up in their conversation?</i>

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.950
<i>The bold type that doesn't read 
the mood, but pretends he just can't?</i>

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.230
<i>The self-centered type that can't read 
the mood, but pretends he just doesn't?</i>

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.160
<i>A hybrid between them?</i>

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.000
I only know one person like that.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.270
Someone who, despite caring what others think,

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.750
views showing that interest as a sign of failure.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.380
Yes.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.730
That is...

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.640
Should we go?

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:58.480
Let's go.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.330
<i>I know. I really do know.</i>

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.890
<i>I'm excessively self-conscious.</i>

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.350
<i>No one really cares what I do.</i>

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.880
<i>No, I'm the one who's 
weird for caring about that.</i>

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.500
<i>Actually, it's caring about it that 
makes me excessively self-conscious.</i>

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.630
<i>I feel like my mind's racing in circles.</i>

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.680
<i>Do I want to care or not?</i>

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.980
<i>Do I want to act like I care or not?</i>

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.920
<i>And </i>should <i>I care or not?</i>

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.300
Makuwa Uriya.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.730
Monster of ego.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.570
You'll make an appropriate 
servant to the Caerula Adamas.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.480
What's going on? Is this a delusion?

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.130
Or a prank?

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.970
No, it must be a delusion.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.960
After all, I'm not exactly famous 
enough to be the subject of a prank.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.200
But what if, by chance, someone films 
this and the video is put on the internet,

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.390
Aurum!

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.060
Argentum!

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.040
Perla!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.800
and this becomes my world debut, 
and I become surprisingly popular?

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.880
Donum!

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:51.990
That's right!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.430
I'm not some ordinary gourd <i>(uri)</i>, 
but a special melon!

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.610
Yes, a muskmelon!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.740
<b>Earth Defense Club                        (lol)</b>

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.120
Hey!

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.830
So who came up with the name 
"Earth Defense Club," anyway?

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.090
Who knows? It's been called that 
since I started coming here.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.120
Well, not like it matters.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.820
If it doesn't matter, don't ask.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.080
Yufuin-senpai, is that manga interesting?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.400
Occasionally.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.140
Which means it's usually boring, then?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.650
Sounds like your relationships with girls.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.060
Occasionally interesting.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.170
The memories are priceless.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.150
Don't make me laugh.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.720
I'm impressed you two can hang out.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.460
<i>You're</i> saying that, Yufuin-senpai?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.120
What does that mean?

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.840
You mean me and En-chan?

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.520
Speaking of which, why 
do you hang out with me?

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.120
<i>You're</i> asking that?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.050
Yeah.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.050
Why...? It just went that way, I guess?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.950
Wow. That's mean.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.580
You asking me why was pretty mean, too.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.020
Well, to me, Atsushi, you're basically air.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.720
Is that a compliment?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.150
It's a huge compliment.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.720
Is it?

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:10.390
Yo!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.980
Why are you coming in from there?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:13.930
And down!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.830
I think a change of mood is a good thing sometimes.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.220
What do you mean, change of mood?

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.650
I'd really like to hear about this.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.240
Just kidding. It's a joke.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.300
It's because Wombat ran away!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.780
He should just give up and 
surrender himself to you already.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.030
That's right!

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.810
What do you even like about that bristly thing?

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.370
He stinks, too.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:37.460
I am not bristly, nor do I stink!

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.210
Oh, now look! Wom-san is pouting! Poor thing!

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:45.050
Well, <i>I'm</i> still on your side, okay?

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:50.240
But if Yumoto was chasing you, 
why did you show up after he did?

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:53.020
And where's Mr. Tawarayama?

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.220
Did you leave him again?

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.320
He's right here!

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.570
Hey, rigor mortis is setting in!

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.540
Who hung that bag on him?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.190
Oh, that's mine!

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:08.240
I wish you'd share a hundredth of the concern 
you have for Wombat with Mr. Tawarayama.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.580
It's the Love Alert!

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.790
I'm sick of arguing about 
whether we should go or not.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.260
Might as well just go.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.260
Let's zip over there and zip right back.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.210
Stop treating this like a rush job!

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.140
There he is!

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.480
I've been waiting, Battle Lovers!

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.270
You, who befoul our beloved Earth!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.020
No justice can come from loveless power!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.270
Love is all!

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.780
Live for love! Die for love!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.900
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.440
Battle Lovers!

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.210
Feel the power...

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.620
Of love!

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.280
Now, let's go right to the Love Attack!

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.450
Why don't we have a little talk?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.010
A talk? About the jealousy, envy, 
and inferiority you feel towards us?

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.890
Yes, that might make a good theme.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:10.550
Jealousy, pity, and envy are three of a kind, 
cooking poison in the same pot.

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.890
What? Is today's monster a wannabe scholar?

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.050
Epinard, I leave this sort of 
self-sufficient type to you.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:19.800
Huh? Why?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.020
It seems like your strong point.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.130
I'll beat him down with my 
unique communication skills!

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.240
You can't call it communication 
if you're trying to beat him down.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.780
First, we have to be quiet and hear his side.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.780
Huh? Grumble grumble.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.760
Don't say "grumble grumble."

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.830
So what do you have to say?

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:44.340
The "Andes" in "Andes melon" doesn't 
refer to the Andes Mountains.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:46.160
<b>Scroll of 
Riddles</b>

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.180
Did you know that?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.450
The "Andes" in "Andes Melon" doesn't 
refer to the Andes Mountains.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.550
The truth is...

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.760
Yeah? Yeah?

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:56.160
The "Prince" in "Prince melon"
doesn't refer to royalty.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.220
The truth is...

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.310
Yeah? Yeah?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.780
Melons are not really fruit. The truth is...

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.220
Yeah? Yeah?

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.310
Are you interested?

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:10.400
If you want to know the truth, you'll 
have to come to Mt. Binan on Sunday.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:15.100
We shall meet again, friends of my soul!

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.610
What, you're not gonna tell us now?

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.740
No fair!

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.120
The "Andes" in "Andes melon"

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.500
comes from "anshin desu" (don't worry)
with the core (shin) removed.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.380
A play on the fact that it's a melon with seeds.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.250
Wow!

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.860
The "Prince" in "Prince melon"

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.900
is named after the group that 
developed the seeds in a lab.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:35.720
Wow!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.080
"Fruit," according to the Ministry 
of Agriculture and Forestry,

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.760
is something that grows into a tree,

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.160
whereas melons are herbaceous, 
growing at the soil level,

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.480
which makes them fruit-like vegetables.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.600
Wow!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.770
By the way, the "musk" in "muskmelon"

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:53.250
doesn't come from the fact 
that it appears to have a mask,

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:54.110
You can look up anything on 
the internet nowadays, huh?

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.620
but because it produces a 
strong aroma known as "musk."

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.320
And that monster seemed so confident 
as it threw those riddles at us.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.320
Wow! Wow!

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:02.150
One other thing: the mesh pattern 
of a muskmelon is scars!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:06.500
It's because of fractures that occur in 
the rind as the fruit within is growing.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.250
Wow!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:12.520
I wish the monster could have seen that "Wow!"

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.590
He probably would've been 
pretty pleased with himself.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.140
He probably thought he could lure 
out someone like Yumoto that way.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.350
Lure me out? What do you mean, Io-senpai?

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:26.320
Yumoto, you really are carefree.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.320
Listen to me. The enemy's plan is...

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.700
To set a trap for them and strike!

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.530
That is our plan this time!

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.890
We've been one step 
behind them all this time.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:39.400
This time, we shall annihilate the enemy.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.990
It's a truly delicious idea.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.730
By the way, Lord Zundar.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:49.490
Is that thing you're eating right now a sn—

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.480
Is that escargot?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.870
No, it's a snail!

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:57.720
The foods of Earth are delicious.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:01.570
This time, at last, our victory is assured!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.810
An ambush?!

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.390
What a lovelessly dirty trick!

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.270
Regardless of the ambush, 
just getting there would be a pain.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.750
You mean you guys aren't planning to go?

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.950
You're saying you <i>are</i> planning to go?

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:21.290
Well, he did say, "We shall meet again!" 
We solved his melon riddles, but still...

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.860
How far are you willing 
to go to humor someone?

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.460
It's not like we told him we'd go, so we're safe.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.000
That's right.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:28.630
What?

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.300
Wait a minute!

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:33.140
The heirs to the throne of love, 
the Battle Lovers, can't simply—

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:36.680
But it'll be tiring, and baths cost money.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.390
You can't spend money you don't have.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.350
Why are you looking at me?

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:46.400
I think Wombat's trying to 
ask you to pay our way there.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.540
Now, look...

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:51.320
If you try to borrow money from Io, 
your friendship with him is over.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:54.780
In this situation, I suppose that cannot be helped.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:55.970
In the name of love—

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.660
Are you saying friendship isn't love?!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.820
In that case, I know a very good way!

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:06.920
<b>Arima Ibushi
Born November 10th
Blood Type AB / Scorpio
Hobbies: Backgammon
Likes: Gardening,
carbonated rice crackers</b>

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.500
Ugh, it's you! Where did you come from?

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.560
How rude of me!

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.410
I overheard your conversation.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:19.420
Overheard...?

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.710
If you're having money troubles,

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:25.140
our Press Society feels it is of 
<i>pressing</i> urgency to come to your aid!

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:28.720
Press Society...

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.190
...and pressing urgency?

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:31.060
Was that a joke?

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.700
We have a very good idea.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.980
A surefire way to make a fortune in no time!

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:37.600
What is it?

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.380
Do you remember?

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:44.460
Our Press Society published your Earth
Defense Club activities on the internet.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.380
Well, yeah...

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.070
That's right, that did happen.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.660
That article was a big hit!

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.170
Yumoto-kun's cuuuuuute!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.680
Yes, he's an angel!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.680
En is way too hot

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.680
Atsushiiiiiiiiii

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:54.170
Right now, you all are internet idols!

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.170
Io-kun Io-kun Io-kun Io-kun

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.170
Yumoto-kun Yumoto-kun Yumoto-kun

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.170
I love glasses!

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:55.920
Huh?!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.900
Internet idols?

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.170
Isn't that term a little vague?

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.940
I know the words "internet" and "idols,"

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.390
but when you put them together, 
suddenly it all feels very indeterminate.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.690
Don't think about it too hard!

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:12.310
The point is, you're popular!

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:18.670
I've received a lot of requests for more 
coverage of that five-man hottie group!

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.410
You want us to do something 
to Mr. Tawarayama again?

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:26.740
No, no, no! I'm speaking more of gravure.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.330
Gravure?!

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:31.670
If you agree to be my models...

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.250
I could probably pay you this much.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:37.690
No way!

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.540
That's not possible! 
Are you trying to scam us?

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.630
Do not underestimate your own popularity!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.900
If you sell well, I might be
able to pay you even more!

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.840
Wow!

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.840
Then, first, take these.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:57.530
Good! Good! Yumocchan, you're amazing!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.790
Oh, am I?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.000
Magnum!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.180
Great shot!

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:03.120
Perfect!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.450
Was the Press Society photographer 
always that kind of character?

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:08.240
A little bit of blur...

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.410
And now, the rest of you!

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:20.200
Good! Nice! Yes, straighter!

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.760
Right! Good!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.920
Wait! This is all just cosplay!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:29.140
It's part of a plan to put pictures of the 
Earth Defense Club wearing various costumes

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.800
in calendars and sell them like hotcakes!

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.200
Who would buy something like that?

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:39.080
You know, it's like those calendars with 
burly firemen and athletes in various poses.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.750
I've heard of those.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.910
I feel vaguely like I've sold my soul.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.880
Money talks, even in hell.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.050
Well, would you like your receipt?

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.080
As thanks for the photos.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:03.690
Those Press Society guys are really great!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.110
These rice balls are delicious!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.650
Thanks, big bro!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.780
Cards! I wanna play Old Maid!

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:11.030
Then we'll play shiritori!

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.340
And the Yamanote Line game!

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.750
Oh, there's not enough time!

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:16.180
He's sure excited.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.050
Damn, persistent caller.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:19.460
Did something happen?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.880
The air is so fresh!

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.440
We finally made it.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:43.380
<b>Binan Mountain Station</b>

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:32.780
She doesn't believe I'm really 
away on club business.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.320
That's only natural.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.970
That's so cold! Take a selfie with me, okay?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.130
Sure, but won't she think it's 
just a badly shopped photo?

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:47.630
Girls are cute, but they're 
really annoying at times.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.050
Really? At times?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:53.440
Well, I think of the annoyance 
as part of their cuteness.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.990
Amazing.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.270
Anyway, so we have to climb this?

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:05.660
If someone says to meet on Mt. Binan, 
they'd normally mean the summit, right?

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:08.870
Can we transform?

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:12.200
Oh? Have you finally recognized 
yourselves as the Battle Lovers?

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.520
No, but our physical skills increase 
when we transform, right?

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.790
I thought it'd make it a little easier.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:21.250
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.710
Battle Lovers!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.670
Feel the power...

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.900
Of love!

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.060
Or so I thought, but I guess not.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:38.450
En-chan, you never exercise effort, 
spirit, or endurance, do you?

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.140
Yeah. I'd rather be a lifetime idler.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.660
That was close! What is this thing?

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.650
A sinkhole, maybe?

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.380
Now I'm even more tired.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:55.090
By the way, Atsushi, what do 
you want to do in the future?

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:58.030
Me? I'm not sure.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.030
Go to college and get a job
like most people, I guess?

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:02.550
Io, are you going to the Cayman Islands?

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:05.610
There's no retiring from 
investment and management, after all.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.770
Well, I'm gonna become Hugh Hefner!

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.440
I don't know about that.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.910
I'm gonna become the world's 
#1 bath-firewood man!

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.820
Isn't your family's pubilc bath a <i>natural</i> hot spring?

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:19.830
That's true, but "bath-washer man" 
doesn't have as nice a ring to it.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:21.980
What is all this, anyway?

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:25.360
Hey!

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:28.470
Hey, Melon Monster!

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.570
We're here!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.780
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.600
You told us to come!

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:40.240
Well, yes, but on the way up, I set all those...

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.850
Oh, you mean that survival action stuff?

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.020
That was pretty fun! Thanks!

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:49.540
No, I don't think he put 
those there for us to enjoy.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:50.880
Oh, really?

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:54.980
You may be my enemy, but I am impressed!

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:56.790
Looks like he bounced back.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.850
You must be very interested in 
the melon riddles I threw at you.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.070
Yeah. Actually, we figured 
them all out using the internet.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:05.460
What?!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:09.000
"Anshin desu," the name of a group, 
and fruit-like vegetables.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.400
Also "musk" and scars.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.920
It can't be... No...

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.570
You solved my melon riddles so easily?!

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.140
Also, sorry...

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.720
I'm the kind of person who doesn't really 
care if he gets melon after dinner or not.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:22.570
Same here, actually.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:24.090
It's just another gourd, anyway.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.740
I prefer cherries.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:29.060
Not American cherries, but Sato Nishiki.

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:30.960
Those are more expensive too, right?

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:34.920
<i>It can't be... You don't care about melons?</i>

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.770
It's melon, you know? <i>That</i> melon!

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:40.110
Sorry.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:42.220
If you give me some, I <i>will</i> eat it, of course.

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.690
What an apathetic reaction!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.020
You've shaken my entire raison d'etre!

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.360
He's suffering.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.890
Really suffering.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:55.030
Why are you talking about 
"raison d'etre," anyway?

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.500
J-Just kidding. I knew that, too.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.870
The melon is a relic of the past.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:03.130
I was just playing melon.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.130
Because they say melons are tops, you know?

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.330
Playing melon? Melons are tops?

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.060
In the same way bananas started 
to sell out in an instant,

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:15.440
and the way people started to say that eggs 
are the honor student of foodstuffs,

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:19.760
even thinking of melons as 
having value is a total anachronism.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.760
Is this guy okay? He's getting 
into self-abuse now...

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:21.980
I knew all that,

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:25.450
but when you say that, it just makes
people worry about you, you know?

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.060
So the melon was just playing melon!

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.770
Who is he even talking to?

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.690
Himself, I think?

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.520
He seems desperate to bounce back from this.

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:36.910
I'm not special at all,

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:40.150
but whether you're expecting 
me to be special or not,

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.430
I'd still like to meet your expectations, 
or something like that.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.500
Have you ever met someone so willing to 
think things down two or three levels?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.510
Or something like that!

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.320
What's he talking about?

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:54.120
In a word, he's excessively self-conscious?

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:55.500
That's likely.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.760
Likely?!

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:03.330
I don't really understand, but don't sweat it.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:04.960
No worries!

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:05.930
No worries?!

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.350
That's right. We did come, after all.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.610
You took pity on me!

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:15.200
This is a nice place. I'm glad we came.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.570
We owe you, Melon Monster.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:21.730
If not for you, I would never have 
given a second thought to melons.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:23.280
I'm glad.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:28.790
I like melon-flavored shaved ice and such.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:30.800
And melon bread.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.290
And melon soda, too.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.890
The cheap stuff has its own appeal.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.250
And everything has its own flavor.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:51.810
So you don't mind a melon like me?

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.020
Why would we mind?

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.080
Everyone, now! Give him love!

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:03.460
Love Shower!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.450
Ah, the synergistic effect 
of comfort and healing!

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:15.500
100% fruit juice is soaking into my scars!

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.750
I don't need to stay in a 
paulownia box any longer!

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:24.220
Love is over!

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.310
The presence has disappeared.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:29.730
So he's been loved, as well?

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.120
A shame.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:33.590
Forgive us, Lord Zundar.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.520
It seems our selection was ill-considered.

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:38.480
But it did have a bit of an effect.

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:39.940
Effect?

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:43.630
Let's be satisfied with what we did for today.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:49.450
After we take a brief rest, 
we'll consider our next development.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:52.240
With that, I bid thee farewell!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.420
It looks like the gravure was popular.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:02.370
I hope this will translate into numbers, as well.

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:03.890
Right?

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:43.060
Isn't it true that the more a person
thinks of himself as "cute,"

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:45.440
the blacker his heart must be?

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:46.900
How do I know that's true?

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:50.260
Well, it's true of me, after all!

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:53.310
Next time: Love is Glasses...

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:55.160
Next Time

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:55.160
Love is Glasses...

00:23:53.310 --> 00:23:54.560
Conquest!
